      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "The regression requires model no3/po4 stored per volume (mol m-3) to be converted to micromoles per kilogram at 1025 kg/m3, while WOA23 is per mass, so the differing scale factors must be applied correctly before any comparison.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Archived `no3`/`po4` are per volume (mol m-3); to get µmol kg-1 convert with µmol kg-1 = mmol m-3 × 1000 / ρ (× 1e6/ρ from mol m-3). Never relabel a ×1000 prefix change as \"µmol/kg\".",
        "N:P is invariant under a common density factor, so the mean-of-ratio and ratio-of-means values need no density; only the regression's µmol kg-1 concentrations do. The question prescribes ρ = 1025 kg m-3 constant, whereas the fragment asks for in-situ density (`compute_potential_density_anomaly`, `ref_pressure=None`) and warns the constant errs ~1% — the question's constant is followed and the difference stated."
      ]
    },
