      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "The percentage-of-water-volume metrics (N:P 14–18 and N:P<12) and any volume weighting require volcello, whose definition as tracer-cell volume and relation to areacello/deptho must be handled correctly.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The 200-1000 m layer thickness and volume weights come from `volcello` / `areacello` (`cell_thickness_like`), the only form that respects partial bottom cells; `lev_bnds` differences fail there (GFDL-ESM4: 1.53e18 vs 1.33e18 m3, 14% of cells off by >1%).",
        "Use each model's own `areacello`/`volcello` and report `attrs['area_source']` and `attrs['volume_source']`; do not rescale one model's area to match another's."
      ]
    },
    {
