      "reason": "The \"percentage of water volume\" metrics and any domain means must be volume-weighted over all ocean cells using the native grid rather than treated as unweighted spatial averages.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "All layer means are volume-weighted: Σ x·volcello / Σ volcello over valid cells, i.e. `op='volume_weighted_mean'`; the mean of the cell-by-cell N:P and the ratio of the two volume-weighted means are different quantities — the question reports both, labelled.",
        "Volume percentages of N:P between 14-18 and below 12 come from `compute_exceedance_fraction` (NaN-aware, returns the m3 behind the %), not from a share of cells; missing cells stay out of the denominator."
